            <ArticleTitle>Twisting wire technique: An effective method to retrieve fractured guide wire fragments from coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>282-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2016.01.013</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(16)30062-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With the increasing number of complex coronary interventions, there has been an increase in the incidence of device fractures and dislodgements. We report 2 cases of successful retrieval of fractured guide wire fragments from coronary arteries using the twisting wire technique and discuss its advantages and issues.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2016. Published by Elsevier Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
